        "original_id": "edc7e009-6951-5245-9f31-c487fba7344c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Betzy Kjelsberg\n- Places: Svelvik, Vestfold, Norway, Buskerud, Telemark\n- Organizations: Liberal Party\n- Roles: politician, board member, factory inspector\n- Topics: feminist movement, county\n\nFacts:\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was born as Betzy Aleksandra Børresen on 1 November 1866.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was born in Svelvik in Vestfold, Norway.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was a Norwegian politician for the Liberal Party and a member of the feminist movement.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was the first female board member of the Liberal Party.\n- From 1910 to 1936, Betzy Kjelsberg served as Norway's first female factory inspector.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg died on 3 October 1950.\n- Vestfold is a county in Norway.\n- Vestfold borders Buskerud and Telemark.",
